{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789237449,"nonce":"0/q6tdDd7gyknrrGcrPYQH8VvCk=","title":"Cranelift AsyncLoadSlot ignores the slot's type when it is not already in the type cache","message":"An async frame slot is stored as i64 and narrowed on load to the slot's\nHIR type via `type_cache.get(ty)`, defaulting to I64 when the type is\nmissing. The cache is primed from Binary, Cast, Load and a few other\ninstructions, not from AsyncLoadSlot itself, so a slot whose type appears\nnowhere else in the function (an i32 parameter used only in an i64\nexpression) is loaded as i64 while HIR says i32. Any later instruction\nthat trusts the HIR type (`sext` of the slot) fails verification.\n\nSurfaced when the SSA builder started widening mixed-width integer\noperands (eb8be0d): `async fn double(x: i32) i32 { return x * 2 }` now\nemits `sext %x` and the poll function was skipped, failing nine embed\nasync tests.\n\nFix: prime type_cache from AsyncLoadSlot too.","files":null}]}